WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:00.875
To sum up.

2
00:00:00.875 --> 00:00:05.975
You read the reader's role, collected two
incidents and then saw both close, showed

3
00:00:05.975 --> 00:00:11.075
that only one kind ever arrives, and watched
the kit refuse a call nobody verified.

4
00:00:11.075 --> 00:00:15.154
The evidence an ISSO keeps for
Gate 5 is the raw Google response,

5
00:00:15.154 --> 00:00:19.939
the notices as JSON and as a spreadsheet
file, and the manifest, all dated;

6
00:00:19.939 --> 00:00:24.960
the role binding; and the written gaps:
no planned maintenance through the A P I,

7
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:30.137
and any workload in a package that doesn't
include Personalized Service Health.

8
00:00:30.137 --> 00:00:33.212
Before you ship, work through
the chapter's checklist.

9
00:00:33.212 --> 00:00:35.400
That finishes the five providers.

10
00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:38.525
Next is Module 7: routing to owners.

11
00:00:38.525 --> 00:00:43.837
It takes the notices every provider produced,
and gives the ones that need action an

12
00:00:43.837 --> 00:00:48.740
owner, a severity and a due date, as typed
tasks in the service desk's front door.
